   },
   "dwc:habitat": {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "This species lives attached to rocks and coral rubble, often between 0.5–3.0 m. Sometimes isolated polyps may occur (Verrill 1900). As other species closely related, this species has a tendency to form carpets, often intermingled with species of Zoanthus, which can grow between stolons and polyp clusters (Ryland & Lancaster 2003) (Fig. 4b)."
   },
   "dwciri:substrate": {
